---
import UtilityPage from '../layouts/UtilityPage.astro';
const documents = [
  ['Photograph', 'Follow the current portal’s live-photo or uploaded-photo instructions. Do not assume that an older CEN uses the same process.', '/photo-resizer/?preset=rrb-photo'],
  ['Signature', 'Sign on plain paper in the required ink. Match the file type, dimensions, and KB range shown in your upload field.', '/rrb-signature-resize/'],
  ['Class 12 marksheet / certificate', 'Keep the original ready. Upload a scan only if requested; preserve the board name, roll number, marks, and all page edges.', '/document-resizer/?preset=marksheet-12th'],
  ['SC / ST and other category documents', 'Use the certificate format and validity rules specified in CEN 07/2026. Choose PDF only when the field accepts it.', '/document-resizer/?preset=caste-certificate'],
];
---
<UtilityPage title="RRB NTPC Undergraduate Document Checklist" description="CEN 07/2026 preparation for 12th-level applicants: signature scans, Class 12 certificates, category documents, and fixes for common upload problems.">
  <section class="rounded-2xl border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-5 space-y-3"><p class="text-xs font-bold text-primary tracking-wider">CEN 07/2026 · UNDERGRADUATE / 12TH LEVEL</p><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Keep the graduate and undergraduate notices separate</h2><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">The published undergraduate notice reports 1,688 posts and an application window from October 15 to November 13, 2026 (23:59 IST). CEN 06/2026 is a separate graduate-level recruitment. Check the latest RRB notice and any extension before applying.</p><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-xs font-semibold"><a class="text-primary underline" href="https://rrb.indianrailways.gov.in/patna" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official RRB notice listing</a><a class="text-primary underline" href="https://indianexpress.com/article/education/rrb-ntpc-ug-notification-2026-out-rrb-indianrailways-gov-in-applications-open-1688-posts-10922540/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dates and vacancies: published report, Oct 15</a><a class="text-primary underline" href="https://www.rrbapply.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RRB application portal</a></div></section>
  <section class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">{documents.map(([title, description, href]) => <article class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 space-y-3"><h2 class="font-bold">{title}</h2><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{description}</p><a class="text-primary text-sm font-semibold" href={href}>Prepare image →</a></article>)}</section>
  <section class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 space-y-3"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">If a file is rejected</h2><ol class="list-decimal pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2"><li>Read the upload field’s exact format and minimum/maximum KB limits. General document presets are starting points, not official RRB specifications.</li><li>Check the downloaded file’s bytes, pixels, and extension. Renaming a PNG to JPG does not convert it.</li><li>Inspect small text and seals at 100% zoom. Reduce shadows or rescan rather than repeatedly compressing an unreadable image.</li><li>Reopen the exported file before uploading and keep the unedited original.</li></ol></section>
  <a class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary" href="/admit-card-photo-print-sheet/">After applying: prepare your exam-day photographs →</a>
</UtilityPage>
